[{:db/id 17592186129215 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-37b63c9c-6c92-5f44-bb20-4d23e2c51ff4" "question-6d75b243-8939-5146-b57c-2c5e64292e74"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129217 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-394bc722-72f5-5959-b491-d15c78d36cfd" "question-5eff5095-a0c0-5448-9e3d-e45ec11b1792"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129216 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b3f52ad3-220f-5e23-b87e-dca64195a02f" "question-e501ffe3-f914-5273-b8d8-73d2e5bc3adb"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-37b63c9c-6c92-5f44-bb20-4d23e2c51ff4" :question/id #uuid "37b63c9c-6c92-5f44-bb20-4d23e2c51ff4" :question/math-academy-id "q-126523" :question/problem "Consider the arc of the curve $y=x-{x}^{4}$ that lies between the lines $x=0$ and $x=1.$ What integral gives the surface area generated when this arc is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis?" :question/worked-solution "We can find the surface area generated when a curve is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis using the formula\n\n$$\nS=\\int 2\\pi y\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a curve in the form $y=f(x),$ we have \n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we will use\n\n$$\nS=2\\pi {\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe are told that the limits of integration are from ${x}_{1}=0$ to ${x}_{2}=1.$ \n\nComputing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x-{x}^{4})=1-4{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-{x}^{4})\\sqrt{1+{(1-4{x}^{3})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-{x}^{4})\\sqrt{2-8{x}^{3}+16{x}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-59d98658-24fe-5433-bf3d-9f4ab64a837f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-59d98658-24fe-5433-bf3d-9f4ab64a837f" :answer-field/id #uuid "59d98658-24fe-5433-bf3d-9f4ab64a837f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f9a7b159-f3eb-5808-a9b3-9de83766c488" :answer-field/choices ["answer-32cf01df-92ff-5fdb-a4e6-5c90197c9574" "answer-f9a7b159-f3eb-5808-a9b3-9de83766c488" "answer-7f585402-a8df-55bb-b2ab-4ae33bb5202f" "answer-076d4f91-52ee-5265-9716-346105e7c17c" "answer-3a00d32e-d7d5-5b7b-ae72-6a9a030e3ace"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-32cf01df-92ff-5fdb-a4e6-5c90197c9574" :answer/id #uuid "32cf01df-92ff-5fdb-a4e6-5c90197c9574" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-{x}^{4})\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f9a7b159-f3eb-5808-a9b3-9de83766c488" :answer/id #uuid "f9a7b159-f3eb-5808-a9b3-9de83766c488" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-{x}^{4})\\sqrt{2-8{x}^{3}+16{x}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7f585402-a8df-55bb-b2ab-4ae33bb5202f" :answer/id #uuid "7f585402-a8df-55bb-b2ab-4ae33bb5202f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}{(x-{x}^{4})}^{2}\\sqrt{2-8{x}^{3}+16{x}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-076d4f91-52ee-5265-9716-346105e7c17c" :answer/id #uuid "076d4f91-52ee-5265-9716-346105e7c17c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-{x}^{4})\\sqrt{1-4{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3a00d32e-d7d5-5b7b-ae72-6a9a030e3ace" :answer/id #uuid "3a00d32e-d7d5-5b7b-ae72-6a9a030e3ace" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-{x}^{4})\\sqrt{2-8{x}^{3}+16{x}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6d75b243-8939-5146-b57c-2c5e64292e74" :question/id #uuid "6d75b243-8939-5146-b57c-2c5e64292e74" :question/math-academy-id "q-126540" :question/problem "![](images/68/68a30adbe260a15c8514ceec2291da4be77af2335f8999d512ffd46c7b18c6bc.png)\n\nConsider the arc of the curve $y=2x-{x}^{2}$ that lies in the first quadrant between its $x$-intercepts. What integral gives the surface area generated when this arc is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis?" :question/worked-solution "We can find the surface area generated when a curve is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis using the formula\n\n$$\nS=\\int 2\\pi y\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a curve in the form $y=f(x),$ we have \n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we will use\n\n$$\nS=2\\pi {\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to determine the limits of integration. To do this, we find where the curve intersects the $x$-axis by solving the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-{x}^{2} & =0 \\\\ x(2-x) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we need to integrate from $x=0$ to $x=2.$ \n\nComputing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2x-{x}^{2})=2-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}(2x-{x}^{2})\\sqrt{1+{(2-2x)}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}(2x-{x}^{2})\\sqrt{5-8x+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fab2c55e-07fe-5e9d-9f01-1f1219cae67d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fab2c55e-07fe-5e9d-9f01-1f1219cae67d" :answer-field/id #uuid "fab2c55e-07fe-5e9d-9f01-1f1219cae67d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e4f8c068-5bb0-55aa-83b2-528951078bbf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c95d3b99-6b88-52d5-97b3-f7bcc08f66b4" "answer-71a555ef-03a3-57cb-9c25-d34ed5de385c" "answer-e4f8c068-5bb0-55aa-83b2-528951078bbf" "answer-51c26f7f-96ba-5d02-b426-27fbbc8d3851" "answer-d9ef6e77-7117-5a21-9fbc-23ba538a199d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c95d3b99-6b88-52d5-97b3-f7bcc08f66b4" :answer/id #uuid "c95d3b99-6b88-52d5-97b3-f7bcc08f66b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}(2x-{x}^{2})\\sqrt{2-2x+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-71a555ef-03a3-57cb-9c25-d34ed5de385c" :answer/id #uuid "71a555ef-03a3-57cb-9c25-d34ed5de385c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}(2x-{x}^{2})\\sqrt{1-8x+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e4f8c068-5bb0-55aa-83b2-528951078bbf" :answer/id #uuid "e4f8c068-5bb0-55aa-83b2-528951078bbf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}(2x-{x}^{2})\\sqrt{5-8x+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-51c26f7f-96ba-5d02-b426-27fbbc8d3851" :answer/id #uuid "51c26f7f-96ba-5d02-b426-27fbbc8d3851" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}{(2x-{x}^{2})}^{2}\\sqrt{5-8x+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d9ef6e77-7117-5a21-9fbc-23ba538a199d" :answer/id #uuid "d9ef6e77-7117-5a21-9fbc-23ba538a199d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{2}{(2x-{x}^{2})}^{2}\\sqrt{1-8x+4{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-394bc722-72f5-5959-b491-d15c78d36cfd" :question/id #uuid "394bc722-72f5-5959-b491-d15c78d36cfd" :question/math-academy-id "q-109146" :question/problem "Consider the arc of the curve $x=\\sqrt{y}$ that lies between $y=1$ and $y=4.$ What integral gives the surface area generated when this arc is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis?" :question/worked-solution "We can find the surface area generated when a curve is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis using the formula\n\n$$\nS=\\int 2\\pi y\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a curve in the form $x=f(y),$ we have \n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we will use\n\n$$\nS=2\\pi {\\int }_{{y}_{1}}^{{y}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nWe are told that the limits of integration are from ${y}_{1}=1$ to ${y}_{2}=4.$ \n\nComputing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\sqrt{y})=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {\\int }_{{y}_{1}}^{{y}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{4}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{4}y\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{4y}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{4}y\\sqrt{\\frac{4y+1}{y}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{y(4y+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0e573e19-5887-51da-bc0d-a02e833ab7a9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0e573e19-5887-51da-bc0d-a02e833ab7a9" :answer-field/id #uuid "0e573e19-5887-51da-bc0d-a02e833ab7a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-75065807-d394-54ee-9589-a02778ac1b06" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6a63776c-a3e2-5252-b4f9-f985fc644009" "answer-92a3d043-6533-553c-a302-61c4dbd94b5b" "answer-358a047c-5548-544e-bf1d-f9959f75de54" "answer-75065807-d394-54ee-9589-a02778ac1b06" "answer-f074a450-1ea5-5e8e-b2c1-3c16ad93c9d6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6a63776c-a3e2-5252-b4f9-f985fc644009" :answer/id #uuid "6a63776c-a3e2-5252-b4f9-f985fc644009" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{4y+1}}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-92a3d043-6533-553c-a302-61c4dbd94b5b" :answer/id #uuid "92a3d043-6533-553c-a302-61c4dbd94b5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{4y+1}}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-358a047c-5548-544e-bf1d-f9959f75de54" :answer/id #uuid "358a047c-5548-544e-bf1d-f9959f75de54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{4y+1}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-75065807-d394-54ee-9589-a02778ac1b06" :answer/id #uuid "75065807-d394-54ee-9589-a02778ac1b06" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{y(4y+1)}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f074a450-1ea5-5e8e-b2c1-3c16ad93c9d6" :answer/id #uuid "f074a450-1ea5-5e8e-b2c1-3c16ad93c9d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi {\\int }_{1}^{4}y\\sqrt{4y+1}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5eff5095-a0c0-5448-9e3d-e45ec11b1792" :question/id #uuid "5eff5095-a0c0-5448-9e3d-e45ec11b1792" :question/math-academy-id "q-109186" :question/problem "![](images/a7/a70a12201e99ded8eed85b797c760862814e1f0a50129020fa6d3b35d4334394.png)\n\nConsider the arc of the curve $x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y$ that lies in the first quadrant between its $y$-intercepts (see figure above). What integral gives the surface area generated when this arc is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis?" :question/worked-solution "We can find the surface area generated when a curve is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis using the formula\n\n$$\nS=\\int 2\\pi y\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a curve in the form $x=f(y),$ we have \n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we will use\n\n$$\nS=2\\pi {\\int }_{{y}_{1}}^{{y}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to determine the limits of integration. To do this, we find where the curve intersects the $y$-axis by solving the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & =0 \\\\ y & =\\pm n\\pi ,\\,n\\in Z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we need to integrate from $y=0$ to $y=\\pi .$ \n\nComputing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {\\int }_{{y}_{1}}^{{y}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }y\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡y}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-cd353f17-4f1a-5904-b62b-8c4277a7e856"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-cd353f17-4f1a-5904-b62b-8c4277a7e856" :answer-field/id #uuid "cd353f17-4f1a-5904-b62b-8c4277a7e856" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c6975ddc-3a08-5688-b3d1-0de4aad419be" :answer-field/choices ["answer-93561cb9-31e8-5f50-b3bf-ac1e4c078018" "answer-b0993602-e32e-5385-8615-215b677568b2" "answer-9e7a244a-9ef8-56e4-ad31-1e3ad490a401" "answer-c6975ddc-3a08-5688-b3d1-0de4aad419be" "answer-c21c3926-fbd8-543d-9a89-059162436863"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-93561cb9-31e8-5f50-b3bf-ac1e4c078018" :answer/id #uuid "93561cb9-31e8-5f50-b3bf-ac1e4c078018" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}y\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡y}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b0993602-e32e-5385-8615-215b677568b2" :answer/id #uuid "b0993602-e32e-5385-8615-215b677568b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}y\\sqrt{1+{sin}^{2}⁡y}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9e7a244a-9ef8-56e4-ad31-1e3ad490a401" :answer/id #uuid "9e7a244a-9ef8-56e4-ad31-1e3ad490a401" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡y}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c6975ddc-3a08-5688-b3d1-0de4aad419be" :answer/id #uuid "c6975ddc-3a08-5688-b3d1-0de4aad419be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }y\\sqrt{1+{cos}^{2}⁡y}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c21c3926-fbd8-543d-9a89-059162436863" :answer/id #uuid "c21c3926-fbd8-543d-9a89-059162436863" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }y\\sqrt{1+{sin}^{2}⁡y}\\,\\text{d}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b3f52ad3-220f-5e23-b87e-dca64195a02f" :question/id #uuid "b3f52ad3-220f-5e23-b87e-dca64195a02f" :question/math-academy-id "q-126580" :question/problem "Consider the arc of the curve $y=\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}$ that lies between the lines $x=0$ and $x=1.$ Calculate the surface area generated when this arc is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "We can find the surface area generated when a curve is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis using the formula\n\n$$\nS=\\int 2\\pi y\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a curve in the form $y=f(x),$ we have \n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we will use\n\n$$\nS=2\\pi {\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe are told that the limits of integration are from ${x}_{1}=0$ to ${x}_{2}=1.$ \n\nComputing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}})=-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,⇒\\,{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{1-{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi x\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =2\\pi (1-0) \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c6c197bd-bdee-548f-8f17-1f8666979616"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c6c197bd-bdee-548f-8f17-1f8666979616" :answer-field/id #uuid "c6c197bd-bdee-548f-8f17-1f8666979616" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a5fc830d-ddfb-52ef-95a5-7275134c641b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a5fc830d-ddfb-52ef-95a5-7275134c641b" "answer-9643975e-56c0-5fb2-ba93-036c9d01f4c4" "answer-cd696a17-23bd-5ea8-84ec-8d71128b61db" "answer-0cba0bba-3874-5f31-9506-90e69f99ee58" "answer-3f9acf2a-3897-5212-ae15-bafc3627e866"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5fc830d-ddfb-52ef-95a5-7275134c641b" :answer/id #uuid "a5fc830d-ddfb-52ef-95a5-7275134c641b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9643975e-56c0-5fb2-ba93-036c9d01f4c4" :answer/id #uuid "9643975e-56c0-5fb2-ba93-036c9d01f4c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd696a17-23bd-5ea8-84ec-8d71128b61db" :answer/id #uuid "cd696a17-23bd-5ea8-84ec-8d71128b61db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0cba0bba-3874-5f31-9506-90e69f99ee58" :answer/id #uuid "0cba0bba-3874-5f31-9506-90e69f99ee58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3f9acf2a-3897-5212-ae15-bafc3627e866" :answer/id #uuid "3f9acf2a-3897-5212-ae15-bafc3627e866" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e501ffe3-f914-5273-b8d8-73d2e5bc3adb" :question/id #uuid "e501ffe3-f914-5273-b8d8-73d2e5bc3adb" :question/math-academy-id "q-109269" :question/problem "Consider the arc of the curve $y=\\sqrt{x}-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3/2}$ that lies between the lines $x=0$ and $x=3.$ Calculate the surface area generated when this arc is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "We can find the surface area generated when a curve is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis using the formula\n\n$$\nS=\\int 2\\pi y\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a curve in the form $y=f(x),$ we have \n\n$$\n\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we will use\n\n$$\nS=2\\pi {\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe are told that the limits of integration are from ${x}_{1}=0$ to ${x}_{2}=3.$ \n\nComputing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x}-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3/2})=\\frac{1-x}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\,⇒\\,{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}=\\frac{1-2x+{x}^{2}}{4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =2\\pi {\\int }_{{x}_{1}}^{{x}_{2}}y\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{3}(\\sqrt{x}-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3/2})\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1-2x+{x}^{2}}{4x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{3}(\\sqrt{x}-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3/2})\\sqrt{\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}(3-x)}{3}(\\frac{x+1}{2\\sqrt{x}})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(3-x)(x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(3+2x-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\pi {[3x+{x}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =3\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a8e6cbf3-7b66-5401-9a6d-5259b70ef31f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a8e6cbf3-7b66-5401-9a6d-5259b70ef31f" :answer-field/id #uuid "a8e6cbf3-7b66-5401-9a6d-5259b70ef31f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5f5eaa2f-7b67-59fb-ac74-96008538d1e1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-422bd46c-effb-5d0b-904d-3ee35544d973" "answer-5f5eaa2f-7b67-59fb-ac74-96008538d1e1" "answer-53183f8e-14d6-52c2-9f1a-70be683a7846" "answer-a548f782-4430-54c1-9ade-29c1fd806b51" "answer-c743a931-9156-5119-af96-2e6b26ebadfb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-422bd46c-effb-5d0b-904d-3ee35544d973" :answer/id #uuid "422bd46c-effb-5d0b-904d-3ee35544d973" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f5eaa2f-7b67-59fb-ac74-96008538d1e1" :answer/id #uuid "5f5eaa2f-7b67-59fb-ac74-96008538d1e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53183f8e-14d6-52c2-9f1a-70be683a7846" :answer/id #uuid "53183f8e-14d6-52c2-9f1a-70be683a7846" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a548f782-4430-54c1-9ade-29c1fd806b51" :answer/id #uuid "a548f782-4430-54c1-9ade-29c1fd806b51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c743a931-9156-5119-af96-2e6b26ebadfb" :answer/id #uuid "c743a931-9156-5119-af96-2e6b26ebadfb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129339 :activity/expected-seconds 1260.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
